ha Hadid's extension (2005) bending away to the northwest; Snøhetta's largely underground galleries (2021) shown by the glittering angular skylights in the lawn. From Ordrupgaard's own architecture page, Dezeen and ArchDaily descriptions. Refined 29 Sep 2026 (no photographs reachable): Hadid's wing, which was a row of upright boxes along its arc (a black wall with a flat roof), rebuilt as a continuous shell of black lava concrete — twenty mitred segments whose roof runs from its high glazed inner edge, facing the lawn, down to about a metre at its outer edge, so roof and outer wall read as one sloping surface, with the glass wall the whole length of its inner side; the park's old beeches given their different sizes. The voxel coarsened from 0.8 to 0.9 m (the plate was 125 across and the new shell nearly 28,000 dots; now about 22,700) with every box snapped to the grid. Guessed: the orientation, which way Hadid's wing runs, its width (about 9.5 m) and heights, the render colour and every size (the OpenStreetMap ground is sketchy here)."}